Export the OF match table so the module autoloads.

The vendor kernel builds rknpu in-tree and never needed the alias;
as an out-of-tree module, without MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, ...) there
is no of: alias in modules.alias and udev/nerves_uevent cannot load
the driver for the 27700000.npu platform device at boot.

Signed-off-by: Isaiah DeRose-Wilson <isaiahdw@gmail.com>

--- a/rknpu_drv.c
+++ b/rknpu_drv.c
@@ -313,6 +314,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id rknpu_of_match[] = {
 	},
 	{},
 };
+MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, rknpu_of_match);
 
 static int rknpu_get_drv_version(uint32_t *version)
 {
